{"id":"f8aa6496-dbc0-43c6-bcee-2f03d74e041a","object":"chat.completion","created":1793847766,"model":"deepseek-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"I'll inspect the logger module header (imports) before editing.\n\n```python\nprint(read_range(\"deepinfer/logger.py\", 1, 35)[\"content\"])\n```","reasoning_content":"Let me check the current state of the files, particularly environ.py around the Logging section, and logger.py fully, and stats_logger.py worker. I have previous evidence. Let me read the relevant portions again to make edits (evidence is already registered). Let me read logger.py lines 1-33 and 33-107, stats_logger relevant, and environ Logging section.\n\nActually evidence shows the whole environ.py content (lines 1-221) in ev-22d3... which is the full file. Good. And logger.py portions. Let me read logger.py 1-33 and check module-level variables to know imports.\n\nWe need to do edits now. Let me plan the implementation.\n\n### environ.py\n\nAdd a factory method or use envs class attribute:\n\n```python\n    # -- Logging --\n    DEEPINFER_LOGGING_INTERVAL_STEP = EnvVar.int(default=100)\n    ...\n```\n\nAdd:\n```python\n    DEEPINFER_LOG_MAX_MESSAGE_CHARS = EnvVar.log_max_message_chars()\n```\nHmm, requirement: \"可增加必要标准库辅助函数，但保留原配置项、描述符类已有成员和刷新函数；描述符类可以新增辅助工厂方法（用于创建配置项的方法）\". So add a helper function `_log_max_message_chars(v)` or a factory method `int_or_none_min`. Simplest: add module-level helper function `_optional_int_min(v, minimum)` and class attribute `EnvVar(lambda v: _log_max_message_chars(v))`. But note: the Value error must contain the variable name; EnvVar.__get__ wraps exception as type(e)(f\"{self.name}: {e}\") — so raising ValueError(\"must be >= 32\") gets prefix DEEPINFER_LOG_MAX_MESSAGE_CHARS. Good.\n\nAdd helper:\n\n```python\ndef _log_max_message_chars(v: str | None, minimum: int = 32) -> int | None:\n    if v is None:\n        return None\n    try:\n        value = int(v)\n    except (TypeError, ValueError):\n        raise ValueError(f\"expected an integer >= {minimum}, got {v!r}\") from None\n    if value < minimum:\n        raise ValueError(f\"expected an integer >= {minimum}, got {v!r}\")\n    return value\n```\n\nNote: empty string: int(\"\") raises ValueError -> wrapped. Good.\n\nThen:\n```python\n    DEEPINFER_LOG_MAX_MESSAGE_CHARS = EnvVar(_log_max_message_chars)\n```\nWait, `_log_max_message_chars` takes one arg, so EnvVar accepts it directly as init callable. But also `@EnvVar` decorator style? Factory method allowed. I'll use `EnvVar(_log_max_message_chars)`? That's within class body: module-level function referenced. Fine.\n\nBut \"描述符类可以新增辅助工厂方法（用于创建配置项的方法）\" — optional. Could add static method:\n\n```python\n    @staticmethod\n    def log_max_message_chars() -> EnvVar[int | None]:\n        return EnvVar(_log_max_message_chars)\n```\nEither fine. I'll add both helper function and a factory method for clarity? Keep minimal: helper function + class attr using EnvVar(...). That's acceptable.\n\n### logger.py\n\nNeed to read the top of logger.py for imports. Read lines 1-35.\n\nFormatting: NewLineFormatter __init__ signature add `max_message_chars: int | None = None` keyword-only? \"保留原有四个位置参数，新参数 max_message_chars 只能按名称传入\" — so `def __init__(self, fmt, datefmt=None, high_precision=False, use_color=False, *, max_message_chars=None)`. Validate: not bool, isinstance int, >=32 else ValueError.\n\nIn format(), need to compute truncated message after args substitution but not modifying record. Approach: use `record.getMessage()` to get substituted message; but base formatter uses record.message set by super().format. The requirement: \"先完成 %s 等参数替换，再计算消息长度\" and \"不能改写共享原记录的 msg、args、exc_info、stack_info\". We can compute truncated message and then format with a lightweight approach: create the message via record.getMessage(), then format using the format string. But easiest and safe: use `copy`? No copy import maybe. We can construct the formatting ourselves:\n\n```python\ndef format(self, record):\n    original_message = None\n    if self.max_message_chars is not None and getattr(record, \"keep_full_message\", False) is not True:\n        message = record.getMessage()\n        if len(message) > self.max_message_chars:\n            record.message = self._truncate(message)  # mutating record.message?\n```\n\nMutating record.message is technically record attribute change; requirement forbids msg, args, exc_info, stack_info. `record.message` is set by formatter anyway. But subsequent handler (stats full) needs full message — the record is shared across handlers! If we set record.message truncated, the next handler's formatter (maybe same default handler? stats use same handler) would... Actually the default handler is the only handler; stats messages pass keep_full_message so not truncated. But a normal message handed to a \"full handler\" later — tests might have two formatters attached to handlers and check the second full. Mutating record.message would break it. Safer: don't mutate; compute the formatted string ourselves then post-process.\n\nApproach: temporarily substitute? Better: build using base Formatter with a proxy? Standard trick:\n\n```python\ndef format(self, record):\n    formatted = super().format(record)\n    if budget allows and not keep_full:\n        full_msg = record.message  # set by super().format as getMessage()\n        if len(full_msg) > budget:\n            truncated = self._truncate_message(full_msg)\n            # Replace the message occurrence in formatted output\n```\n\nBut formatting includes exception text and stack_info appended after message. We need to limit only message body, not exception traceback. `formatted` is prefix + message + exception text. Could compute prefix = formatted up to message start? Original code does `prefix = msg[: msg.find(record.message)]`. But `msg.find` could find message earlier in prefix (e.g., levelname?). Hmm.\n\nSimpler robust approach: temporarily swap `record.msg` and `record.args`? That mutates shared record — forbidden (but could restore). Requirement says cannot rewrite the shared record's msg/args. Even temporarily is risky.\n\nAlternative: format with overridden record.message. In logging.Formatter.format:\n\n```python\nrecord.message = record.getMessage()\nif self.usesTime(): record.asctime = ...\ns = self.formatMessage(record)\nif record.exc_info: ...\n```\n\nIf record.message exists, it reassigns it. So we can't inject truncated message via record.message without mutation.\n\nBetter: compute truncated message ourselves, then temporarily create a shallow copy of the record using `copy.copy(record)`. Is copy allowed? Standard library import allowed (course says \"可增加必要标准库导入\"). We can import copy in logger.py. A shallow copy doesn't modify the original record; setting attributes on the copy is fine. That satisfies \"不能改写共享原记录\". Use:\n\n```python\ndef format(self, record):\n    if self.max_message_chars is not None and getattr(record, \"keep_full_message\", False) is not True:\n        message = record.getMessage()\n        if len(message) > self.max_message_chars:\n            record = copy.copy(record)\n            record.message = None??? \n```\n\nBut copy.copy shares msg and args (fine, we don't change them). We replace: set `record.msg = truncated; record.args = ()` on the copy. That's clean: the copy's msg/args replaced; original untouched. Then call super().format(record). Note `record.message` from previous handler may exist on shared record; copy carries it, then Formatter recomputes message = record.getMessage() from copy's msg/args. Good.\n\nActually we could avoid copy by setting copy's message attribute only — but Formatter overwrites record.message = record.getMessage(). So set msg/args.\n\nSo:\n\n```python\ndef format(self, record):\n    if self.max_message_chars is not None and getattr(record, \"keep_full_message\", False) is not True:\n        message = record.getMessage()\n        if len(message) > self.max_message_chars:\n            record = copy.copy(record)\n            record.msg = self._truncate_message(message)\n            record.args = ()\n    msg = super().format(record)\n    ...\n```\n\nCareful: `record.getMessage()` calls str(msg) % args if args. If args is a dict etc, getMessage handles. If msg is not str and args is None, getMessage returns str(msg). Then setting record.msg to a string and args=() is fine.\n\nEdge: getMessage can raise if formatting errors? original would too; base Formatter catches? Actually Formatter.format calls record.getMessage() directly, so same behavior.\n\nTruncation marker: `...<omitted>...` length 15? \"...\" 3 + \"<omitted>\" 9 + \"...\" 3 = 15. Budget 32 -> remaining 17, head = ceil(17/2) = 9, tail = 8. Spec example: \"预算32时，保留开头9字符、末尾8字符，加上15字符标记\" - yes head = ceil(remaining/2), tail = remaining - head.\n\n```python\n_MESSAGE_OMITTED = \"...<omitted>...\"\n\ndef _truncate_message(message, budget):\n    remaining = budget - len(_MESSAGE_OMITTED)\n    head = (remaining + 1) // 2\n    tail = remaining - head\n    return message[:head] + _MESSAGE_OMITTED + message[len(message) - tail:]\n```\n\nIf budget >=32, remaining >=17 > 0. Good.\n\nValidation in init:\n\n```python\nif max_message_chars is not None:\n    if isinstance(max_message_chars, bool) or not isinstance(max_message_chars, int) or max_message_chars < 32:\n        raise ValueError(...)\n```\n\nNote for invalid value, error message maybe include param name. Fine.\n\n`_setup_logger()` passes `max_message_chars=envs.DEEPINFER_LOG_MAX_MESSAGE_CHARS`. Need import in logger.py: from deepinfer.environ import envs. Check logger.py imports; read top.\n\n### stats_logger.py\n\nIn `_log_worker`, change `logger.info(m)` to `logger.info(m, extra={\"keep_full_message\": True})`.\n\nNow let's read logger.py top and confirm imports and env usage elsewhere to avoid circular imports. Let me read logger.py lines 1-35.\n\nAlso check if logger.py already imports envs.\n\nLet's do read_range."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":10133,"completion_tokens":2364,"total_tokens":12497,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":4096},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":2325},"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":4096,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":6037},"system_fingerprint":"bc19ba97cbe016479903222bb1578db6"}